h incorrectly accepted it as a character despite explicit instructions to reject beverages\n   194→  - The LLM (qwen2.5:32b) is not reliable for distinguishing common nouns from character names\n   195→  - Confidence: HIGH\n   196→\n   197→**Changes Made:**\n   198→- File: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/validator.py`\n   199→- Lines 24-29: **Added** `FOOD_BEVERAGE_NAMES` set with common food/drink names including 'amontillado', 'wine', 'sherry', etc. (24 entries total)\n   200→- Lines 164-176: **Added** pre-filter check to reject food/beverage names BEFORE LLM validation\n   201→- This is a heuristic filter similar to the existing `PLACE_NAMES` filter (line 142)\n   202→\n   203→**Smoke Test Results (PASS):**\n   204→```\n   205→✓ \"Amontillado\" → REJECT (food/beverage)\n   206→✓ \"Wine\"        → REJECT (food/beverage)\n   207→✓ \"Sherry\"      → REJECT (food/beverage)\n   208→✓ \"Fortunato\"   → ALLOW\n   209→✓ \"Montresor\"   → ALLOW\n   210→```\n   211→\n   212→**Full Test Suite: PASSED**\n   213→- 444 tests passed, 11 skipped, 1 warning\n   214→- No regressions introduced\n   215→\n   216→**Issues Addressed:**\n   217→- ✅ Issue #1: \"Amontillado\" (a wine) is listed as a character\n   218→- ⏳ Issue #2: Montresor not identified as narrator (should cascade from fixing #1)\n   219→- ⏳ Issue #5: Plot summary uses \"Amontillado\" as narrator name (should cascade from fixing #1)\n   220→\n   221→**Expected Impact:**\n   222→- Amontillado should be filtered out before character extraction completes\n   223→- Narrator detection should then correctly identify Montresor (since Amontillado won't be competing)\n   224→- Plot summary should use correct narrator name\n   225→\n   226→## Output Files (Attempt 3)\n   227→- HTML: output/cask_of_amontillado/report.html\n   228→- JSON: output/cask_of_amontillado/analysis.json\n   229→\n   230→## Pipeline Notes (Attempt 3)\n   231→- Analysis completed successfully in 7m 12s\n   232→- Structure: 1 chapter detected\n   233→- Ch