Poe.txt\",\n    \"source_format\": \"txt\",\n    \"total_word_count\": 2358,\n    \"total_character_count\": 13023,\n    \"estimated_total_duration_minutes\": 15.693333333333333,\n    \"words_per_minute\": 150\n  },\n  \"structure\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"chapter\",\n      \"title\": null,\n      \"index\": 1,\n      \"start_position\": 24,\n      \"end_position\": 13023,\n      \"word_count\": 2354,\n      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 15.693333333333333,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"children\": [],\n      \"characters_present\": [\n        \"Montresor\",\n        \"Fortunato\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the narrator, Montresor, declaring his intent to exact perfect revenge on Fortunato for an unspecified insult, vowing to punish him with impunity. During the chaotic carnival season at dusk, Montresor lures the drunken, costumed Fortunato—wearing a jingling motley outfit—into the damp, bone-strewn catacombs beneath his palazzo under the pretense of tasting a rare pipe of Amontillado. Guided by Montresor, they descend through labyrinthine vaults, where Montresor feigns concern for Fortunato’s cough, offering wine to ease the dampness, while subtly manipulating him deeper into the crypt. Once in a secluded niche lined with human remains, Montresor chains Fortunato to the wall and begins sealing him alive behind a brick wall, all while Fortunato initially laughs, thinking it a jest, until his cries turn desperate. Montresor completes the wall, silencing him, and leaves the body entombed for over fifty years, ending with a hollow 'In pace requiescat.'\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_fortunato_b564181f\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"Fortunato\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Fortunato is a man whose pride in his experti