pt, exploiting Fortunato’s pride and love of wine to ensure his compliance.\n\nThe rising action unfolds as Montresor leads Fortunato into a secluded niche lined with human remains, a place of isolation and dread. Here, Montresor reveals his true intentions by chaining Fortunato to the wall, a moment that marks the turning point of the story. Initially, Fortunato laughs, convinced the act is a joke, but as Montresor begins to build a brick wall to seal him in, his laughter turns to desperate pleas and cries. Montresor remains cold and methodical, continuing his work with quiet precision, even as Fortunato’s terror becomes palpable. The psychological torment of being buried alive, combined with Montresor’s calm demeanor, underscores the depth of his calculated cruelty and the tragic irony of Fortunato’s misplaced trust.\n\nThe climax occurs when Montresor completes the wall, sealing Fortunato behind it, leaving him trapped and silent. Montresor then steps back, satisfied that his revenge is complete and that he has achieved his goal of punishment with impunity. The final act of the story is Montresor’s return to the site after more than fifty years, where he delivers a hollow, ironic blessing: 'In pace requiescat'—'May he rest in peace.' This closing line underscores the story’s chilling tone and Montresor’s enduring obsession with his crime, suggesting that his guilt, if any, is buried as deeply as Fortunato’s remains. The narrative concludes with Montresor’s retrospective account, revealing a man who has lived with his dark secret for decades, unrepentant and unburdened by remorse.</div>\n                \n                <p style=\"margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--muted);\">\n                    <strong>Themes:</strong> revenge, madness, deception\n                </p>\n                \n            </section>\n            \n\n            \n            <section>\n                <h2>🤖 Analysis Models</h2>\n                <table style=\"width: 100%; margin-top: 1rem