ta)\n- ✅ **Amontillado NOT in character list** - Fixed from previous attempts!\n- ✅ No false character merges\n- ✅ No hallucinated characters\n\n**Critical Issue:**\n- Montresor only has 1 mention_count, but he IS the narrator - every \"I\" in the text refers to him. This is an NER limitation (documented in previous attempts).\n\n**Score: 7/10**\n- Missing Luchresi (-1.5 points)\n- Montresor's mention_count of 1 is technically correct (his name only appears once when Fortunato cries \"For the love of God, Montresor!\") but the system should recognize him as narrator and attribute first-person statements to him (-1.5 points)\n\n---\n\n### 2.3 Character Profiles (Weight: 15%)\n\n**Fortunato:**\n- Has description text ✅\n- Description captures his pride in wine expertise ✅\n- Description accurately describes his arc from confidence to terror ✅\n- confidence: \"low\" (noted in low_confidence_items)\n\n**Montresor:**\n- ❌ **NO descriptions** - empty `descriptions` array\n- ❌ **NO relationships** - empty object\n- ❌ **NO evidence** - empty array\n- ❌ `is_narrator: false` - but the plot_summary correctly identifies him as narrator\n\nThe narrator issue is concerning - the `is_narrator` field is false for both characters, yet the plot_summary correctly identifies Montresor as the first-person narrator. This is an inconsistency.\n\n**Score: 5/10**\n- Fortunato profile is decent but low confidence\n- Montresor has essentially no profile despite being the protagonist/narrator\n- `is_narrator` field is incorrect for Montresor\n\n---\n\n### 2.4 Chapter Summaries (Weight: 20%)\n\n**Chapter 1 Summary (the entire story):**\n\nReading the summary in `structure[0].summary`:\n\nThe summary is **excellent**:\n- ✅ Accurately captures Montresor's intent for revenge\n- ✅ Describes carnival setting correctly\n- ✅ Describes Fortunato's costume (motley, jingling bells) accurately\n- ✅ Describes the wine cellar/catacomb setting correctly\n- ✅ Captures the key events: luring, descent through vaults, chaining, bricking up\n- ✅ Captures emotional arc: Fortunato's initial laughter, then terror\n- ✅ Ends with correct detail: 50+ years, \"In pace requiescat\"\n- ✅ No hallucinated events\n- ✅ Appropriate length (~200 words)\n\nThe plot_summary in `overview.plot_summary.plot_summary` is even more detailed and accurate:\n- ✅ Correctly identifies Montresor as first-person narrator\n- ✅ Captures themes: revenge, manipulation, calculated cruelty\n- ✅ Mentions key details: Amontillado wine as lure, pride in wine expertise as weakness\n- ✅ Accurate ending with Latin phrase\n\n**Score: 9/10** (Excellent summary quality)\n\n---\n\n### 2.5 Pronunciation Guide (Weight: 10%)\n\n**Expected:** Foreign words, unusual proper nouns, period terms\n\n**Flagged words (56 total):**\n\n**Good catches:**\n- ✅ Fortunato (Italian name) - with IPA\n- ✅ Montresor (French name) - with IPA  \n- ✅ Amontillado (Spanish wine) - with IPA\n- ✅ Luchresi (Italian name) - with IPA\n- ✅ flambeaux (French plural) - with IPA\n- ✅ nitre (British spelling)\n- ✅ roquelaire (French cloak)\n- ✅ \"Nemo me impune lacessit\" (Latin motto) - both \"impune\" and \"lacessit\" flagged\n- ✅ requiescat (Latin)\n- ✅ De Grave (French wine region)\n- ✅ puncheons (archaic term for barrels)\n- ✅ rheum (archaic/medical term)\n\n**False positives (common words that shouldn't be flagged):**\n- ❌ jingled - common English verb\n- ❌ filmy - common English adjective\n- ❌ orbs - common English noun\n- ❌ leer - common English noun/verb\n- ❌ familiarly - common English adverb\n- ❌ recoiling - common English verb\n- ❌ to-day - just archaic spelling of \"today\"\n- ❌ tight-fitting - common compound\n- ❌ web-work - simple compound\n- ❌ use, row, close, house, entrance - these are homographs, so flagging is justified\n\n**Missing:**\n- ❌ \"Medoc\" - French wine region, appears in text but NOT in pronunciation list\n\n**Score: 7/10**\n- Good coverage of genuinely unusual words\n- Too many false positives on common words\n- Missing \"Medoc\" which is more unusual than many flagged words\n- The homograph flagging is actually good (use, row, close, entrance, house)\n\n---\n\n### 2.6 HTML Presentation (Weight: 10%)\n\nBased on the HTML preview:\n- ✅ Clean, professional design with dark theme\n- ✅ Tab-based navigation structure\n- ✅ Responsive design (meta viewport tag)\n- ✅ Proper semantic HTML structure\n- ✅ Modern CSS with custom properties\n\n**Score: 9/10** (Well-designed, functional presentation)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Calculate Overall Score\n\n```\nOverall = (\n    Structure × 0.20 +        9 × 0.20 = 1.80\n    Characters × 0.25 +       7 × 0.25 = 1.75\n    Profiles × 0.15 +         5 × 0.15 = 0.75\n    Summaries × 0.20 +        9 × 0.20 = 1.80\n    Pronunciation × 0.10 +    7 × 0.10 = 0.70\n    Presentation × 0.10       9 × 0.10 = 0.90\n)\n\nOverall = 1.80 + 1.75 + 0.75 + 1.80 + 0.70 + 0.90 = 7.70\n```\n\n**Overall Score: 7.70/10** (threshold: 8.0)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Determine Next Action: FAIL\n\nScore 7.70 < 8.0, so we need to identify issues and document fixes.\n\nThe score improved from 6.10 (baseline) to 7.70 (+1.60 points). This is significant progress. The critical \"Amontillado as character\" issue is FIXED.\n\nLet me now update the evaluation state."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26718,"cache_read_input_tokens":33650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":26718,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0e831fa-2001-44b4-9a86-c8b197b4b43a","uuid":"1ca7248a-cb27-4873-9058-39f84507f7ae"}
